# gx3 two-step time-loop smoke case

This case is copied from `cases/gx3_test/ice_in` for checking whether the
CICE-JAX time loop can advance. It keeps the gx3 grid and physical options.
Only `npt=2`, `diagfreq=1`, and `advection='upwind'` differ from the original
case. Input paths are relative to this case directory and use `CICE/input`
beside the `CICE-JAX` repository. Outputs stay in this case directory.

Run `run.py` with the Python environment containing the CICE-JAX dependencies.
It changes into its own case directory and writes `cice.runlog` plus `history/`
and `restart/` output. No Fortran executable or MPI setup is needed.

This is a smoke test of the B-grid/upwind path. It does not validate numerical
agreement with the default remap scheme or CNOP gradients.
